# DTF tier manifest: proxy-downloadcount  (PKT-F, P6 — issue #2537)
# Profile-set: filesystem / single + upstreams=raworigin (a tiny mock nginx
# origin on the slot's 172.16/12 net returning a marker body for any path).
#
# Feature under test — #2537 proxy-cache first-serve download count: a FIRST
# cold proxy GET of a freshly-cached object must be counted. Pre-fix, the
# authoritative `proxy_cache_artifacts` catalog row was written only by the
# streaming tee AFTER the client drained the body, so the serve recorder found
# no catalog row and the first serve recorded +0 (undercounted by 1). The fix
# (proxy_catalog::record_proxy_download) ensures the catalog row in the same
# statement, so the first serve writes exactly one `proxy_download_statistics`
# row. Discriminator: after ONE cold GET the proxy download count == 1 (RED: 0).
#
# OBSERVABILITY (OQ#4 resolved against candidate-a4d7f9d1): NO HTTP endpoint
# surfaces the proxy first-serve count. `GET /api/v1/admin/downloads`,
# `GET /api/v1/admin/analytics/downloads/trend`, and `GET /api/v1/artifacts/{id}
# /stats` all read the SEPARATE `download_statistics` table (hosted-artifact
# attribution), which the remote pull-through serve path does NOT write. The
# only reader of `proxy_download_statistics` is `proxy_catalog::
# download_count_by_repo`, which is NOT wired to any route in this candidate.
# The count is therefore observable ONLY at the DB surface — this oracle asserts
# it via `docker exec $DB_CONTAINER psql` (the established DTF DB-surface idiom;
# see storage-accounting / sso / upgrade / migration tiers). See MATRIX-ROW.md
# for the filed product-gap note (unwired download_count_by_repo).
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: the oracle drives one admin create + a few proxied
# GET/HEAD calls back-to-back through a single admin; the base default (ON) would
# throttle them. Base default stays ON; a tier that must disable a shipped
# control does so explicitly (design section 2.2), same as proxy-egress.
#
# INTEGRATOR NOTES (shared-file needs — DO NOT edit shared files from this packet):
#   * No new published port: raw-origin is reached container-to-container on the
#     slot's private raworigin net; nothing is host-published, so ports.sh needs
#     no change.
#   * No new run.sh manifest-env passthrough: the only manifest override is
#     RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED, which run.sh already special-cases and exports.
#   * Add `proxy-downloadcount` to run.sh's `all` list: it runs green on the
#     single candidate image, so it can join the one-image `all` run.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem upstreams.raworigin"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
